{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Lesley Gore feels like a natural next choice because I want the familiar sixties pop sound that drew me to AM Gold.",
    "Photographs & Memories fits the warm singer-songwriter listening suggested by Jonathan Edwards and Simon & Garfunkel, while Electric Light Orchestra connects with the melodic pop-rock I enjoy in the Beatles and the Cars."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Greatest Hits Collection, Tornado and The Outsiders give me too little musical context to connect them with my tastes; passing on them reflects uncertainty rather than a definite dislike.",
    "Journey, Lynyrd Skynyrd and Queen fit parts of my listening history, but today I am more drawn to melodic pop and gentle folk than to a larger classic rock collection."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My repeated interest in greatest-hits albums seems to have been treated as a reason to offer more compilations, although whose music they contain matters much more to me.",
    "My classic rock listening seems to carry too much weight compared with the particular melodies, voices and songwriting I want right now."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The connection between AM Gold and familiar sixties pop deserves more emphasis because it explains why Lesley Gore stands out today.",
    "My interest in Jonathan Edwards, Simon & Garfunkel and Melanie suggests an appetite for warm, personal songs that a broad classic rock match does not fully capture."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in older music and compilations, but only some capture the melodic pop and warm singer-songwriter sound I want today."
}"}
